    {
      "brand": "Christopher Ward",
      "brandKey": "christopherward",
      "eventId": "spring-sprang-sprung",
      "kind": "recent",
      "text": "C1 Loco Classic — The Loco Classic takes Christopher Ward's suspended-balance Loco into a classic register: a white ceramic Roman-numeral subdial and exposed free-sprung balance in a 41mm steel case. Its hand-wound CW-003 caliber runs for 144 hours; the Gold version is a 2026 GPHG Petite Aiguille nominee.\nPrice: £4,295 ($5,995) on suede strap; £4,495 ($6,275) on Consort bracelet\n\nSealander Yalos Automatic — A slimmer, dressier Sealander in a 39mm steel case, with a stamped, lacquered dial in Ice Blue, Salt Pink, Sand White or Sea Green. A COSC-certified Sellita SW300-1 automatic sits inside.\nPrice: £1,290 ($1,815) on Vesuvio suede strap; £1,495 ($2,095) on Consort bracelet\n\nC1 Jump Hour XV — A 15th-anniversary reimagining of the C9 Harrison Jumping Hour, with a rhodium-silver guilloché dial, Roman-numeral hour window and blue PVD minute hand in a 39mm steel case. The refined JJ01 automatic jump-hour module marks each hour with an instantaneous jump.\nPrice: $2,495 on Consort bracelet\nAvailability: Sold out; manufacturer waitlist open for any pieces that become available. Limited edition of 300 pieces.\n\nC1 Bel Canto Lucia (On camel fine Italian leather (C01-41APT5-T00O0-MC) or Consort bracelet (C01-41APT5-T00O0-B1)) — Teased by Christopher Ward on November 12, 2026 with a count of the world's bird species, the C1 Bel Canto Lucia turns the Bel Canto's chiming mechanism into a songbird, after the bird Lucia sings of in Donizetti's Lucia di Lammermoor. The bird's beak shows whether the chime is on, and its tail is the hammer for the hourly D note. The 41mm titanium case holds the FS01-2 movement, with 65 hours of reserve.\nPrice: $5,550 (Consort bracelet $5,995)",
      "url": "https://www.christopherward.com/int/watches/dive/Sealander",
      "source": "www.christopherward.com",
